ear partnerships with major financial institutions including Chime, Upgrade, Pathward, and Varo Bank.\n• Integrated with risk platforms like Oscilar to provide embedded fairness tools to their customer networks.\n• Currently serves over 25 banks and fintechs, managing fairness for billions in loan volume.","signal_completeness":"historical_seed"},"problem_quality_3c_json":{"summary_text":"The 'Black Box' Bias Problem: As banks move to AI-driven underwriting, they risk inheriting historical biases that lead to unfair rejection of protected classes.\n\nRegulatory Pressure: Agencies like the CFPB and regulators under SR 11-7 require AI models to be transparent, explainable, and fair.\nManual Inefficiency: Traditional fair-lending audits take months and are based on 'batch' data rather than real-time monitoring.\nThe 'Second Look' Gap: Lenders often lack an automated way to re-evaluate 'near-miss' applicants who are creditworthy but flagged by biased algorithms.","root_cause_depth":"The 'Black Box' Bias Problem: As banks move to AI-driven underwriting, they risk inheriting historical biases that lead to unfair rejection of protected classes.","economic_gravity":"The 'Black Box' Bias Problem: As banks move to AI-driven underwriting, they risk inheriting historical biases that lead to unfair rejection of protected classes.\n\nRegulatory Pressure: Agencies like the CFPB and regulators under SR 11-7 require AI models to be transparent, explainable, and fair.\nManual Inefficiency: Traditional fair-lending audits take months and are based on 'batch' data rather than real-time monitoring.\nThe 'Second Look' Gap: Lenders often lack an automated way to re-evaluate 'near-miss' applicants who are creditworthy but flagged by biased algorithms.","structural_urgency":"The 'Black Box' Bias Problem: As banks move to AI-driven underwriting, they risk inheriting historical biases that lead to unfair rejection of protected classes.\n\nRegulatory Pressure: Agencies like the CFPB and regulators under SR 11-7 require AI models to be transparent, explainable, and fair.\nManual Inefficiency: Traditional fair-lending audits take months and are based on 'batch' data rather than real-time monitoring.\nThe 'Second Look' Gap: Lenders often lack an automated way to re-evaluate 'near-miss' applicants who are creditworthy but flagged by biased algorithms.","persona_clarity":null,"stated_problem_ref":null,"signal_completeness":"historical_seed"},"solution_defensibility_json":{"summary_text":"Fairness-as-a-Service™ Platform\n\nAutomated Bias Testing: APIs that back-test and monitor models in real-time to identify disparate impacts on protected groups.\nSecond-Look Underwriting: An automated system that re-underwrites declined applications to find creditworthy borrowers the primary model missed.\nSR 11-7 Compliance: Auto-generates regulatory-ready documentation, cutting validation cycles from months to days.\nAgentic AI Validation: Independent evaluation tools for AI agents to ensure they remain safe and compliant in financial environments.\nFairness Optimization: Proprietary 'loss functions' that teach models to maximize approvals while minimizing disparity during the training phase.\n\nEnabling financial institutions to increase approval rates (typically 10-20%) and revenue without increasing risk, all while maintaining perfect regulatory compliance.","moat_type":null,"replication_difficulty":null,"compounding_potential":null,"technical_moat_evidence":null,"signal_completeness":"historical_seed"},"market_power_json":null,"core_assumption_json":{"the_linchpin_assumption":{},"risk_dynamics":{},"first_order_questions":{"critical_assumption_interrogation":[{"assumption":"Customers will pay and expand for FairPlay AI's core wedge at venture-scale unit economics.","killer_questions":{"evidence":"What signed contracts or paid pilots prove budget and urgency for FairPlay AI?","behavioral_proof":"What would we observe in customer usage that proves repeat, not one-off, adoption?","failure_boundary":"At what ARR or retention threshold would you declare the GTM hypothesis failed?","contradictory_signal":"What single metric trending wrong would force a strategy reset for FairPlay AI?"}}],"linchpin_questions":{"real_world_evidence":"What third-party or customer-attributable proof de-risks FairPlay AI's main claim?","structural_dependency_test":"Which single integration, partner, or regulatory dependency could stall FairPlay AI if it slips?","market_contradiction":"What incumbent or substitute motion would make FairPlay AI's wedge irrelevant in 18–24 months?"}},"structural_auditor_questions":{"dependency_chain_questions":{"weakest_link_verification":"Which step in FairPlay AI's delivery chain (data, compliance, distribution) is least proven?","unvalidated_step_check":"What assumption in the sales or onboarding funnel has not been stress-tested at scale?","cascade_failure_test":"If the primary acquisition channel degrades, what is the fallback path to quota?"},"failure_mode_questions":["How does FairPlay AI lose to a well-funded incumbent copying the feature set?","What breaks first if hiring or roadmap slips by two quarters?"],"conviction_delta_credibility_questions":["What would increase conviction in FairPlay AI by two points on a 10-point scale in 90 days?"]}},"questions_first_order_json":{"critical_assumption_interrogation":[{"assumption":"Customers will pay and expand for FairPlay AI's core wedge at venture-scale unit economics.","killer_questions":{"evidence":"What signed contracts or paid pilots prove budget and urgency for FairPlay AI?","behavioral_proof":"What would we observe in customer usage that proves repeat, not one-off, adoption?","failure_boundary":"At what ARR or retention threshold would you declare the GTM hypothesis failed?","contradictory_signal":"What single metric trending wrong would force a strategy reset for FairPlay AI?"}}],"linchpin_questions":{"real_world_evidence":"What third-party or customer-attributable proof de-risks FairPlay AI's main claim?","structural_dependency_test":"Which single integration, partner, or regulatory dependency could stall FairPlay AI if it slips?","market_contradiction":"What incumbent or substitute motion would make FairPlay AI's wedge irrelevant in 18–24 months?"}},"questions_structural_json":{"dependency_chain_questions":{"weakest_link_verification":"Which step in FairPlay AI's delivery chain (data, compliance, distribution) is least proven?","unvalidated_step_check":"What assumption in the sales or onboarding funnel has not been stress-tested at scale?","cascade_failure_test":"If the primary acquisition channel degrades, what is the fallback path to quota?"},"failure_mode_questions":["How does FairPlay AI lose to a well-funded incumbent copying the feature set?","What breaks first if hiring or roadmap slips by two quarters?"],"conviction_delta_credibility_questions":["What would increase conviction in FairPlay AI by two points on a 10-point scale in 90 days?"]},"pipeline_summaries":{"problem":"The 'Black Box' Bias Problem: As banks move to AI-driven underwriting, they risk inheriting historical biases that lead to unfair rejection of protected classes.\n\nRegulatory Pressure: Agencies like the CFPB and regulators under SR 11-7 require AI models to be transparent, explainable, and fair.\nManual Inefficiency: Traditional fair-lending audits take months and are based on 'batch' data rather than real-time monitoring.\nThe 'Second Look' Gap: Lenders often lack an automated way to re-evaluate 'near-miss' applicants who are creditworthy but flagged by biased algorithms.","solution":"Fairness-as-a-Service™ Platform\n\nEnabling financial institutions to increase approval rates (typically 10-20%) and revenue without increasing risk, all while maintaining perfect regulatory compliance.","traction":"Funding: $10 Million (February 2025) · $24.5 Million · Infinity Ventures · Investors: JPMorganChase, Nyca Partners, Cross River Digital Ventures, TTV Capital, Third Prime Capital\nMilestones:\n• Reported a 3x increase in revenue and client base throughout 2024.\n• Established multi-year partnerships with major financial institutions including Chime, Upgrade, Pathward, and Varo Bank.\n• Integrated with risk platforms like Oscilar to provide embedded fairness tools to their customer networks.\n• Currently serves over 25 banks and fintechs, managing fairness for billions in loan volume.","founder":"Kareem Saleh — Founder & CEO — Former executive at Zest.ai and SoftCard; served in the Obama Administration managing international investment teams.\nJohn Merrill — Co-founder & Principal Scientist — Mathematician and AI expert; previously a lead scientist at Zest.ai and spent 15 years at Microsoft and Google building ML tools.","assumptions":"Key assumptions for FairPlay AI (historical corpus)."}}$j$::jsonb WHERE id = '1b000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005'::uuid;

