at do not communicate.\nAdministrative Burden: Owners spend hours on manual reconciliation, menu updates, and staff scheduling.\nMissed Revenue: Inefficient reservation systems lead to missed calls and empty tables during peak hours.","root_cause_depth":"Small and medium-sized restaurants are currently forced to manage a 'chaos stack' of disconnected tools.","economic_gravity":"Small and medium-sized restaurants are currently forced to manage a 'chaos stack' of disconnected tools.\n\nFragmented Systems: Separate providers for POS, reservations, payments, and marketing that do not communicate.\nAdministrative Burden: Owners spend hours on manual reconciliation, menu updates, and staff scheduling.\nMissed Revenue: Inefficient reservation systems lead to missed calls and empty tables during peak hours.","structural_urgency":"Small and medium-sized restaurants are currently forced to manage a 'chaos stack' of disconnected tools.\n\nFragmented Systems: Separate providers for POS, reservations, payments, and marketing that do not communicate.\nAdministrative Burden: Owners spend hours on manual reconciliation, menu updates, and staff scheduling.\nMissed Revenue: Inefficient reservation systems lead to missed calls and empty tables during peak hours.","persona_clarity":null,"stated_problem_ref":null,"signal_completeness":"historical_seed"},"solution_defensibility_json":{"summary_text":"AI-Native Operating System for Hospitality\n\nUnified POS & Payments: A single platform for in-person card terminals, online ordering, and Tap to Pay.\nZavo Voice Agents: AI agents that answer the phone, handle reservations, and answer customer queries autonomously.\nAgentic Menu Management: AI that allows staff to make instant menu edits or inventory queries via voice/text.\nAutomated Marketing: AI-driven loyalty campaigns that trigger based on customer spending patterns without manual input.\n\nGiving every independent restaurant its own 'digital workforce' to handle the admin and operations, allowing owners to focus entirely on the guest experience.","moat_type":null,"replication_difficulty":null,"compounding_potential":null,"technical_moat_evidence":null,"signal_completeness":"historical_seed"},"market_power_json":null,"core_assumption_json":{"the_linchpin_assumption":{},"risk_dynamics":{},"first_order_questions":{"critical_assumption_interrogation":[{"assumption":"Customers will pay and expand for Zavo's core wedge at venture-scale unit economics.","killer_questions":{"evidence":"What signed contracts or paid pilots prove budget and urgency for Zavo?","behavioral_proof":"What would we observe in customer usage that proves repeat, not one-off, adoption?","failure_boundary":"At what ARR or retention threshold would you declare the GTM hypothesis failed?","contradictory_signal":"What single metric trending wrong would force a strategy reset for Zavo?"}}],"linchpin_questions":{"real_world_evidence":"What third-party or customer-attributable proof de-risks Zavo's main claim?","structural_dependency_test":"Which single integration, partner, or regulatory dependency could stall Zavo if it slips?","market_contradiction":"What incumbent or substitute motion would make Zavo's wedge irrelevant in 18–24 months?"}},"structural_auditor_questions":{"dependency_chain_questions":{"weakest_link_verification":"Which step in Zavo's delivery chain (data, compliance, distribution) is least proven?","unvalidated_step_check":"What assumption in the sales or onboarding funnel has not been stress-tested at scale?","cascade_failure_test":"If the primary acquisition channel degrades, what is the fallback path to quota?"},"failure_mode_questions":["How does Zavo lose to a well-funded incumbent copying the feature set?","What breaks first if hiring or roadmap slips by two quarters?"],"conviction_delta_credibility_questions":["What would increase conviction in Zavo by two points on a 10-point scale in 90 days?"]},"markdown_rejection_blob":"Historical pass / rejection reasoning 